ontent again until the holidays kickoff  number 2 red dead redemption to his  trailer it's hard to name a developer as  beloved as rock star and it's hard to  name a more anticipated game than red  dead redemption to finally over six  years later we got the first official  trailer for the sequel and it told us  sickly nothing we saw some beautiful  woods and prairies and farm towns and we  heard a character who sounded a lot like  Dutch vanderland a big villain from the  first game red dead redemption 2 is  coming to Xbox one and ps4 and fall 2017  so we'll definitely be seeing more of  the game in the future number one the  Nintendo switch new merchandise new  content and new games are all fine and  dandy but nothing gets the gaming world  excited quite like a new console after  months of rumors and speculation the big  end finally announced the Nintendo  switch with a hip millennial filled  trailer the switch is a hybrid console  you can plug in and play on your big  shiny TV or take the tablet controller  with you on the go the trailer also  teased us with some new games like mario  kart 8 splatoon and what looks like a  new adventure for mario nintendo has a  big presentation planned for january so  we'll be seeing more of the switch very  soon these were the biggest stories of  last month but they're just a small part  of everything that happened to check up  on all the consoles games DLC and other  good stuff stick with GameSpot we've got  all the latest 24 hours a day 7 days a  week all year round
 

